Title:
LSA Whisperer

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- LSA Whisperer is a Windows-focused toolset for interacting directly with LSA/SSPI authentication packages via their internal message protocols rather than higher-level Win32 logon APIs.  
- It targets the problem of opaque, under-documented authentication package RPC/message formats by providing implementations and an interactive CLI to call package-specific functions.  
- It includes support for multiple packages (cloudap + AzureAD plugin, kerberos, msv1_0, negotiate, pku2u, schannel) and partial/unstable support for livessp, negoexts, and the Security Package Manager (SPM).  
- The project is useful for red teamers, pentesters, and security researchers doing Windows authentication internals work, token/credential material research, and Azure AD/CloudAP investigations.  
- It’s interesting because it operationalizes low-level LSA package messaging (often only seen in research/PoCs) into a reusable library + tooling, enabling repeatable experimentation and tradecraft development.

Technical Focus:
- LSA authentication packages and message protocols
- SSPI/Security Support Provider (SSP) internals and SPM interactions
- CloudAP/AzureAD plugin protocol surface (PRT-related functionality)
- Kerberos and MSV1_0 package calls (Windows logon/credential flows)
- Negotiate/NegoEx and package selection/brokering behavior
- C++ tooling + static SSPI library implementation (offline-build friendly)

Use Cases:
- Reverse/understand Windows authentication package message formats and behaviors
- Query/experiment with CloudAP/AzureAD-related authentication artifacts and flows
- Prototype and validate Kerberos/MSV1_0/Negotiate package-call based tradecraft
- Build custom research tooling on top of the included `sspi` static library
- Reproduce and extend prior research on SPM, ARSO/TBAL, and NegoEx-related behaviors

Keywords:
LSA, LSASS, SSPI, SSP, Security Package Manager, SPM, authentication packages, cloudap, AzureAD plugin, PRT, Kerberos, msv1_0, Negotiate, NegoEx, pku2u, schannel, Windows 11 SDK, CMake, Windows authentication internals